   "response_text": "Now let me compute statistics on the validation accuracy to better understand the anomaly:\n\nLooking at the data:\n- **Validation accuracies (all 20 epochs)**: 0.8627, 0.8642, 0.863, 0.8701, 0.8678, 0.866, 0.8642, 0.867, 0.8635, 0.8617, 0.8588, 0.862, 0.865, 0.8633, 0.8599, 0.8595, 0.8642, 0.8629, 0.8617, 0.8648\n- **Mean**: (sum of all values / 20) \u2248 0.8638\n- **Range**: min=0.8588, max=0.8701\n- **Healthy range**: 0.8538\u20130.8599\n\nThe validation accuracy is consistently **above** the healthy range. The healthy range is 0.8538\u20130.8599, and almost all epochs in this run are above 0.8599 (except epochs 10 and 15 which are 0.8588 and 0.8595 respectively).\n\nLet me check if there's a subset evaluation configuration that might be inflating the reported accuracy:",
